# Copy to /etc/llama/llama.env (root:root, mode 600). This is the API key that
# llama-swap enforces on 127.0.0.1:9292 - the backends themselves have no auth
# and bind to localhost only. Since the Langfuse change the LAN-facing door is
# the LiteLLM proxy on :8080, whose master key is set to this same VALUE so
# clients never noticed the move. Rotate by editing this file AND
# /etc/litellm/litellm.env (both keys there), then restarting both services.
LLAMA_API_KEY=replace-me
